  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energy Access Talent Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Energy Access Talent Initiative (EATI) is a project to improve access to talent and build a strong and diverse workforce in the African clean energy sector. It includes a work placement program for 800 young people and work readiness training to equip them with skills to navigate and succeed in their new roles. EATI further seeks to address the under-representation of women in the sector by training 300 women in entry-level or junior positions to prepare them to take on additional responsibilities and position them for an upward career trajectory. EATI will also deliver a mid-management development programme to 400 individuals in managerial positions (50%) women. This seeks to address the challenge of weak middle management, identified by energy access employers as one of their biggest challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
